  "created": "2018-01-28T00:17:08.266Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Lights parented to the head of an avatar get rendered a second time from the position of the head bone. This is likely a side effect of the head tracking system as it happens regardless of where you place the light or whether it is nested inside a subchild of the head.\n\nThis is mainly a problem because the second light will illuminate an ugly little circle on your avatar's chin as it passes through the head mesh.\n\nIn the example image, a single red spotlight is parented to the head of the sdk avatar. However, 2 lights are emitted. The upper light coming from the white sphere is the correct one. The bottom one coming from the head itself is incorrect.",
